{
  "name": "Precision Full-Wave Rectifier (Absolute Value)",
  "description": "A two-op-amp precision absolute-value rectifier that rectifies signals far below a diode drop (no dead-zone, unlike a passive diode bridge). Run a transient with a small (e.g. 100mV) sine that crosses zero — the output is |Vin|, with both half-cycles folded positive and peak ≈ the input peak. A true-RMS / measurement front end. (Validated on ngspice.)",
  "tags": [
    "instrumentation",
    "rectifier",
    "precision",
    "absolute-value",
    "opamp",
    "measurement"
  ],
